+* **Per-mutant deadlines.** With selected test IDs and measured test times, each mutant
+  runs in an owned interpreter with budget `max(2 * sum(test times) + 1, 5)` seconds
+  (unknown test durations default to one second). The deadline includes worker startup,
+  collection, tests and teardown; an exec guardian stops and reaps the worker on timeout
+  or caller exit. Cleanup includes ordinary subprocesses in the owned process group and
+  Leela's nested workers. Deliberately detached user processes (for example POSIX `setsid`)
+  and external side effects are outside this reliability boundary: it is not a sandbox.
+  Clean controls and confirmations use the same budget. No budget is enabled when test
+  IDs or timing data are absent. A timeout verdict is not a call-phase assertion failure.
